@* Counter.razor — Demonstrates event handling and component state.
   CONCEPT: @rendermode InteractiveServer
   - By default, Blazor pages are rendered as static HTML on the server.
   - Adding @rendermode InteractiveServer enables a SignalR connection so that
     button clicks and C# event handlers work in real time in the browser.
   - Without this directive, the button would not respond to clicks.
*@

@page "/counter"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Counter – StudentBasics</PageTitle>

<h1>Counter 🔢</h1>
<p>This page demonstrates <strong>event handling</strong> and <strong>component state</strong>.</p>
<hr />

@* CONCEPT: Razor expressions — @currentCount embeds the C# variable value into the HTML *@
<p class="fs-4">Current count: <strong>@currentCount</strong></p>

@* Show a congratulations message when count reaches a multiple of 10.
   CONCEPT: Conditional Rendering — @if renders markup only when the condition is true *@
@if (currentCount > 0 && currentCount % 10 == 0)
{
    <div class="alert alert-success">🎉 You hit @currentCount — great job!</div>
}

@* Show a warning once the count goes negative.
   CONCEPT: Conditional Rendering with @else *@
@if (currentCount < 0)
{
    <div class="alert alert-warning">⚠️ The count is negative!</div>
}

<div class="d-flex gap-2 mt-3">
    @* CONCEPT: Event Handling — @onclick="IncrementCount" calls the C# method below
       when the user clicks this button. *@
    <button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="IncrementCount">+ Increment</button>

    @* Decrement button — same pattern, different method *@
    <button class="btn btn-secondary" @onclick="DecrementCount">− Decrement</button>

    @* Reset button — demonstrates calling a lambda directly in the @onclick *@
    <button class="btn btn-outline-danger" @onclick="() => currentCount = 0">↺ Reset</button>
</div>

@* CONCEPT: Step input — demonstrates two-way data binding with @bind.
   Whatever the user types in the box is immediately reflected in the 'step' variable. *@
<div class="mt-4">
    <label class="form-label">Step size (change how much each click adds/subtracts):</label>
    <input type="number" class="form-control w-25" @bind="step" />
</div>

@code {
    // 'currentCount' is the component's STATE.
    // Blazor re-renders the component automatically whenever state changes.
    private int currentCount = 0;

    // 'step' controls how much each button click changes the count.
    // It is linked to the <input> element via @bind above.
    private int step = 1;

    // Event handler for the Increment button.
    // Blazor calls this method every time the button is clicked.
    private void IncrementCount()
    {
        currentCount += step;
    }

    // Event handler for the Decrement button.
    private void DecrementCount()
    {
        currentCount -= step;
    }
}

